Findings from the rendered inspection
-------------------------------------
- No rendering, accessibility, RTL, or print defect found by measurement: headings ordered,
  alt text on every figure image, narrow scrollers reachable, print unclipped, all 16 Urdu
  SVG variants geometrically clean, bidi/numerals/embedded Latin (wait time, MCQ, RRQ, ERQ,
  B.Ed, URLs) render without overflow or clipping.
- The fig-U6-7 Urdu defect (see the report's blocking finding) is a CONTENT omission, not a
  rendering failure: the served SVG renders cleanly but carries 19 text elements where the
  English carries 22, one note box where the English carries two, and a leader line
  (M346 348 L286 348) pointing at no box. The rendering instruments report "clean" because
  they measure geometry, not EN-UR parity; the omission was found by byte-level EN/UR text
  comparison (ur-figure-text-dump.txt vs en-figure-text-dump.txt).
- Carried platform advisories that apply equally to the Urdu pages (English-side, G3 X1/X3):
  identical accessible names on the five ERQ rubric-table scrollers and the figure scrollers
  at 360px; table-archetype figures display ~640px against 880-936-unit viewboxes on desktop
  (~7.5px effective body text), while at 360px they render at intrinsic width inside the
  scroller.

